# Auto-rebuild after changes

When you finish a task that changes application source (`src/**`, `electron/**`, `vite.config.ts`, or styles/assets consumed by the app), **rebuild before considering the task complete**.

## What to run

Prefer the fast rebuild (skip mineradio vendor unless mineradio integration changed):

```bash
npm run rebuild
```

If the user needs to see changes in the running desktop app immediately, also restart Electron:

```bash
npm run rebuild:app
```

On Windows PowerShell, chain with `;` not `&&` if needed:

```powershell
npm run rebuild; npx electron .
```

## When to skip

- Docs-only, CI-only, or test-only edits with **no** runtime effect
- Changes already verified through an active `npm run desktop:watch` session the user is running

## When vendor is required

Run full `npm run desktop:dev` only when `vendor/mineradio/**` or `scripts/vendor-mineradio.mjs` changed.

## Do not

- Wait for the user to ask for a rebuild after normal feature/fix work
- Use `npm run build` (installer) unless the user asked to package the app
